- NEW: Extracted the full official op-map from `github.com/sumup/sumup-openapi` `openapi.yaml` (8,789 lines, spec dated Nov-2025 per `aade` example `20251112...`): exactly 2 ops declared `x-scopes: []` (`GetPaymentMethods`, `CreateApplePaySession`); `apiKey` scheme = `type: http scheme: Bearer` (sup_sk_ keys share the Authorization slot with JWTs); `authorizationCode` AND `clientCredentials` flows both at `https://api.sumup.com/token` with a 16-scope map incl. `refunds.write`, `transactions.history`, `user.subaccounts` — this is the registered-app scope model, distinct from `dashboard`/`support_centre`.
- NEW (live probe): `GET /v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/payment-methods` returns **200 `application/json` unauthenticated** — identical static body `{"available_payment_methods":[{"id":"card"}]}` for MC0DE, MH4H92C7 (spec-example codes) AND bogus codes ZZ0000/M00000ZZ, and identically 200 with `Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.value` and a fake `sup_sk_...` key. Falsifies the prior KB claim "API fully gated at gateway / all versioned paths 404" — this route bypasses the gateway auth gate entirely.
- NEW (live probe): 5 control spec ops all still 404 unauth (`/v1/merchants/MC0DE`, `/v2.1/merchants/MC0DE/transactions`, `/v0.1/merchants/MC0DE/members`, `/v0.1/merchants/MC0DE/readers`, `/v0.1/merchants/MC0DE/readers/…/status`, `/v1.1/receipts/txn_123`) — the ungated-200 is endpoint-specific, not global.
- NEW: `CreateReaderCheckout` (`POST /v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/readers/{reader_id}/checkout`) request body exposes `return_url` (format-validated only: error message "must be a valid URL"), an `aade` Greek ERP tax-signature object (`provider_id`/`signature`/`signature_data`), and an `affiliate` object (`app_id`/`key`/`tags`) — first-party money-flow surface not previously cataloged.
- CHANGED: `clientCredentials` at `api.sumup.com/token` now spec-confirmed (was hypothesis only), reinforcing the legacy-grant attack surface.
- NO_DELTA: RFC 9728 static, support_centre allowlist still {openid,classic,offline}, callback oracle still 0 HITs.

STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE
- [PRIO] api.sumup.com/v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/payment-methods, 9.1, IDOR/gate-ease: proves one spec op is served outside the auth gate — business=9 (payment-method config), surface=8 (42-op matrix now fully mapped), gate=10 (no auth at all), cloud=7, tech=8, fresh=10.
- [PRIO] api.sumup.com/token, 7.6, AUTH: clientCredentials flow spec-confirmed with money scopes; staging twin proved this gateway family mis-enforces auth_method.
- [PRIO] api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{checkout_id}/apple-pay-session, 7.2, SSRF: spec shows required `context`(hostname)+`target`(uri) with no evident Apple-domain allowlist; response 200 returns the Apple merchant-session to the caller.

STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES
[HYP] payment-methods endpoint returns REAL per-merchant payment config for any merchant_code once the request carries any valid bearer (token-scope not consulted)
class: IDOR
asset: api.sumup.com/v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/payment-methods
confidence: 60
reasoning: Live probe proves the gateway does not auth-gate this route (200 + static body for bogus codes and fake bearers) while every sibling spec op returns 404 — the route is wired outside the normal token gate, so the per-merchant lookup is the only remaining check; spec declares `oauth2:[]` so even a valid-token request has no scope to block on.
evidence_needed: valid token of merchant A + foreign merchant_code returning a body that differs from the unauth static default (real methods incl. card/acquirer-specific/APM set).
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — with ONE key: (1) unauth baseline `GET /v0.1/merchants/{A}/payment-methods` (static card); (2) `Authorization: Bearer sup_sk_...` same code; (3) foreign code BOLA sweep; compare the three bodies — leak = foreign response differs from static default.
impact: Cross-tenant read of merchant payment-method configuration (storefront "pay online" availability, PSI) — MEDIUM/HIGH.
testability: AUTH_HELPED
[HYP] CreateApplePaySession forwards attacker `target` without host allowlist → cloud-metadata/internal SSRF
class: SSRF
asset: api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{checkout_id}/apple-pay-session
confidence: 48
reasoning: Spec: PUT, `x-scopes: []`, body requires `context` + `target` (`format: uri`), example target = Apple gateway; 200 returns the Apple merchant-session object to the caller. Flow requires a server-side HTTPS request to `target` for `startSession`; whether `target` host is pinned to Apple's gateway is the sole unknown. Route live (GET→404 structured problem+json on the PUT path confirms it is routed).
evidence_needed: 200/302 with `target=http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/` or attacker-observable callback; or a 4xx whose timing/error distinguishes an attempted outbound fetch.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — with own sup_sk_: PUT on own checkout_id `{"context":"sumup.com","target":"http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/"}` then `"target":"https://attacker.tld/probe"`; compare 200/4xx bodies and timing; then same with foreign checkout_id (BOLA).
impact: Metadata/internal fetch from payments stack → IAM creds/instance identity — CRITICAL if confirmed.
testability: AUTH_HELPED
[HYP] Legacy api.sumup.com/token clientCredentials grant accepts client_secret_post for a client that declared basic (un-enforced), minting money-scoped tokens
class: AUTH
asset: api.sumup.com/token
confidence: 52
reasoning: Spec now confirms clientCredentials flow at api.sumup.com/token with 16 scopes incl. refunds.write/transactions.history/user.subaccounts; staging twin (auth.sam-app.ro) proved this gateway family stores token_endpoint_auth_method without enforcing it (secret_basic declared, secret_post accepted); prod /token grant never exercised; route live (OPTIONS 204, wildcard CORS, identity.svc).
evidence_needed: controlled app credentials succeeding under a weaker-than-declared auth method and the minted token passing gateway validation on api.sumup.com.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — POST `grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={own_app}&scope=refunds.write` with secret as basic header vs body vs omitted; replay any minted token on `GET /v1/merchants/{own}` (structured 404 = valid).
impact: Money-scoped token minting for a controlled client deviating from declared auth — CRITICAL if deviant, MEDIUM otherwise.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE
- [PARKED] CreateReaderCheckout `return_url` open-redirect/aade-forgery: `return_url` is only format-validated and is the merchant's own SDK redirect (inherent to model); aade forgery has no unauthenticated discriminator — both speculative without a money-flow token.
- [PARKED] CreateMerchantMember role escalation (`role_manager`): requires `members.write` token and a live tenant; no passive path.
- [FINAL] ranked survivors:
  1. RFC 9728 aud/claim-confusion token validation on api.sumup.com — conf 75, AUTH_HELPED.
  2. payment-methods BOLA (gateway bypass proven live, static-default body) — conf 60, AUTH_HELPED.
  3. apple-pay-session SSRF — conf 48, AUTH_HELPED.
  4. /token clientCredentials weaker-auth mint — conf 52, AUTH_HELPED.

STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION
- [NEXT] HUMAN: One `sup_sk_` key (me.sumup.com/settings/api-keys) unlocks the entire 42-op map; run in one session: (1) `GET /v0.1/merchants/{A}/payment-methods` with and without the key, then foreign `{B}` — leak = body differs from static `{"available_payment_methods":[{"id":"card"}]}`; (2) `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{own}/apple-pay-session` with `target` = attacker host then metadata IP; (3) `POST /token` `grant_type=client_credentials&scope=refunds.write` secret as body; (4) replay minted token on `GET /v1/merchants/{own}` (structured 404 = gateway-valid).

STEP 6 — LEARNING
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED BUSLOGIC @ api.sumup.com/v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/payment-methods: endpoint returns HTTP 200 `application/json` unauthenticated for ANY merchant_code (incl. bogus) with static body `{"available_payment_methods":[{"id":"card"}]}`; 200 identical with garbage and fake `sup_sk_` bearers — route bypasses the gateway auth gate while all sibling spec ops 404; prior "API fully gated at gateway" claim was overbroad (this op excluded). No data leak unauth (static default), so finding stands only as an AUTH_HELPED BOLA precondition + recon fact.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ github.com/sumup/sumup-openapi: full op-map extracted — 42 ops, 2 scope-less (`x-scopes: []`), apiKey=Bearer, both OAuth flows at api.sumup.com/token (16-scope registered-app model incl. refunds.write/user.subaccounts); CreateReaderCheckout carries `return_url` (format-only validation) + `aade` (Greek AADE 1155 tax-signature) + `affiliate` objects; spec-dated Nov-2025.
- [LEARN] REJECTED IDOR @ api.sumup.com/v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/payment-methods: NOT a standalone finding — unauth 200 is a static default with no per-merchant variation across MC0DE/MH4H92C7/ZZ0000/M00000ZZ; no cross-tenant data read without a valid token.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED OATH @ api.sumup.com/token: `clientCredentials` + `authorizationCode` flows BOTH documented at `https://api.sumup.com/token` (authorizationUrl=api.sumup.com/authorize) — legacy gateway pair confirmed in first-party spec; route live with wildcard CORS; only untested gap is grant-time auth_method enforcement (AUTH_HELPED).

STEP 7 — RISK
- [RISK] sumup: 72 — No new reportable bug (payment-methods 200 is a static default; contentful closed). Genuine progress: the full 42-op scope×security matrix is now mapped first-party, one spec op is proven to bypass the gateway auth gate (BOLA precondition), and the legacy /token clientCredentials grant is spec-confirmed — but every material path (payment-methods BOLA, apple-pay SSRF, /token mint, RFC 9728 aud test) still requires one `sup_sk_` key or merchant token (AUTH_HELPED). Program flat until HUMAN provides the key; oracle drift all green.
