STEP 1 — DELTA:
- [CHANGED] `api.sumup.com/v0.1/merchants/{code}/payment-methods`: 200 static `{"available_payment_methods":[{"id":"card"}]}` AGAIN this cycle — the 2026-09-17 20:09 "now 404" recorded by BOTH co-leads at identical timestamp was transient/flapping, not durable; handler is unauth-reachable.
- [NEW] OPTIONS 204 + `access-control-allow-origin` origin-echo is a BLANKET gateway catch-all on all 30 paths (spec paths, /authorize, /token, and a generically-unrouted `/nonexistent-route-xyz/foo`) — OPTIONS cannot discriminate routed vs unrouted; prior "OPTIONS 204 = routed" heuristic is invalid.
- [NEW] GET-level discrimination: every spec path returns byte-identical structured 404 `problem+json` (`developer.sumup.com/docs/problem/404-not-found`) identical to a bogus path; `payment-methods` is the ONLY handler-reachable unauth op and it is param-invariant (amount/currency/code/negative → 200 stub, spec-declared 400 never fires).
- [NEW] `sumup-openapi` repo last synced 2026-09-04 (#73), monthly auto-sync from internal `sumup/apis`, spec == live gateway (28 paths / 44 ops + 3 outbound webhooks) — no unprobed endpoint since inventory; freshness vector dry.
- [NEW] webhooks (`readers.created/deleted` etc.) documented with `url: https://api.sumup.com/v0.1/...` — SumUp→merchant outbound; passive-unreachable.

