## STEP 1 — DELTA
- CHANGED `api.sumup.com/v0.1/checkouts/{id}/apple-pay-session`: GET → structured `problem+json` 404 (gateway-handled, same class as v0.2) — v0.1-vs-v0.2 divergence closed; route is PUT-only, not a discriminator (probed this cycle).
- NO_DELTA all other passive surfaces: RFC 9728 metadata static 200; `payment-methods` stub 200 static `{"card"}`; `/v0.2/.../apple-pay-session` OPTIONS 204 origin-echo; `chat.sumup.com` API surface closed (6 endpoints); JWKS prod/staging ZERO kid overlap.

## STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE
- [PRIO] api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{id}/apple-pay-session, 6.5, SSRF-to-cloud-metadata (a6 b9 t7 g1 c9 f6)
- [PRIO] api.sumup.com protected ops (aud/iss binding), 6.2, JWT validation gap (a5 b9 t7 g2 c6 f7)
- [PRIO] chat.sumup.com/api/conversations/{id}, 4.9, IDOR/transcript (a4 b7 t6 g2 c3 f6)

## STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES
[HYP] apple-pay-session `target` lacks host allowlist → SSRF
class: SSRF
asset: api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{checkout_id}/apple-pay-session
confidence: 65
reasoning: openapi + dev docs confirm server fetches caller-supplied `target` (format:uri) and returns fetched Apple merchantSession JSON. Handler reachable pre-token (foreign/no-token PUT → 404 "checkout not found": handler-gated, not token-gated). Control is solely `target` host restriction to *.apple.com. Unauthenticated GET structured-404 on both v0.1/v0.2 twins confirms route exists at handler level.
evidence_needed: own bearer + own checkout; PUT `target=http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/` and aliyun `http://100.100.100.200/latest/meta-data/` vs control `https://apple-pay-gateway-cert.apple.com/paymentservices/startSession` — status/timing/body divergence.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — control PUT (expect merchantSession/decline) then metadata targets (expect 5xx/timeout/body echo = no allowlist).
impact: SSRF → EC2/aliyun metadata → cross-env creds → full prod compromise (CRITICAL).
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] no request-level aud/iss binding on standardized gateway JWT validation
class: AUTH
asset: api.sumup.com protected ops
confidence: 75
reasoning: RFC 9728 declares sole auth_server=auth.sumup.com with NO audience/resource_scopes field; staging JWTs with attacker-controlled aud+empty scp rejected only at JWKS (ZERO kid overlap) on mcp; on the gateway the only verified seam is key binding. Sig-only validation would accept tokens minted for other SumUp audiences.
evidence_needed: own prod bearer on one read op (GET own /v1/merchants/{own}/persons); aud-mutated and iss-mutated copies → same 2xx = no binding.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — 3 GETs ≤1rps: unmutated, aud-mutated, iss-mutated; compare status.
impact: cross-client/subject authorization confusion; token replay across first-party clients (High).
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] chat conversationId lacks ownership discriminator
class: IDOR
asset: chat.sumup.com/api/conversations/{conversationId}
confidence: 40
reasoning: GET returns .data.events; ids server-assigned/opaque; anonymous GET deterministic 500 (no oracle); transcripts inherently cross-merchant; support_chat client PKCE modern-registered.
evidence_needed: own PKCE session → own conversation 200; adjacent/foreign id → 200 with foreign events.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED — complete /api/sso/login (PKCE S256), GET own conversationId, enumerate adjacent ids ≤0.5rps.
impact: cross-merchant support-transcript read (High).
testability: AUTH_HELPED

## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE
- [PARKED] chat conversationId IDOR (40): no unauth oracle, ids server-assigned/opaque, requires own session + control conversation to discriminate — borderline; parked pending AUTH_HELPED credential set.
- Drop confidence<40: none.
- [FINAL] survivors ranked: (1) aud/iss binding AUTH 75 — highest confidence, clean disambiguation via claim-mutation control; (2) apple-pay SSRF 65 — highest impact; both AUTH_HELPED.
- Rejected: OPTIONS/structured-404 route discrimination (REJECTED BUSLOGIC per KB), payment-methods stub (param-invariant, no oracle) — not re-emitted.

## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION
- [NEXT] HUMAN: obtain one legitimate merchant test bearer (sandbox/own test merchant via program, not live customer data) from bugs.olivermaicher.eu channel to unblock both AUTH_HELPED POCs in order: (1) 3-GET aud/iss mutation control on `GET https://api.sumup.com/v1/merchants/{own}/persons`; (2) control-then-metadata PUT on `https://api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{own}/apple-pay-session`.

## STEP 6 — LEARNING
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ api.sumup.com/v0.1/checkouts/{id}/apple-pay-session: unauthenticated GET → structured problem+json 404, byte-identical handling class to v0.2 twin — no v0.1/v0.2 divergence, route is PUT-only at handler; divergence question closed and archived.

## STEP 7 — RISK
- [RISK] sumup: 25 — single ≤1rps read-only GET executed this cycle; no customer data, own/test IDs only; all live POCs remain AUTH_HELPED-gated on legit test credentials; residual risk unchanged (gateway behavioral drift — payment-methods 200↔404 flapping — tracked, no new exposure).
