## STEP 6 — LEARNING
- **[LEARN]** ACCEPTED OTHER @ gateway.sumup.com: the estate's most PCI-relevant host (SumUp Online Payments Hosted Fields, card entry) was absent from a 28-cycle inventory, because scope was inherited from a 9-host seed list while every sweep since was a *callback-host* sweep. Fix applied: enumerated all 226 CT names and triaged by label, which surfaced it immediately. Breadth gaps hide behind "exhaustive" labels — the same defect as last cycle's wrong-path redirect sweep.
- **[LEARN]** REJECTED OATH @ gateway.sumup.com: hosted-fields postMessage has no `event.origin` validation and posts to wildcard `"*"`, and the page is framable by any origin — but with no `Set-Cookie` and all credentials supplied by the embedding parent (trusted by design), no trust boundary is crossed. Framability + wildcard postMessage without demonstrated privilege gain is hardening, not a finding.
- **[LEARN]** REJECTED AUTH @ pos.sumup.com: "SumUp Back-Office" on third-party `sumup.gastrofix.com` is a dormant static SPA — `/api/*` 503 (backend not deployed), all client routes 404. A client-bundle route name (`/login/impersonate`) is a UI label, not a reachable endpoint.
- **[LEARN]** REJECTED OTHER @ soap.sumup.com: CNAME `internal-sumup-live-soap-int-alb-...elb.amazonaws.com` is publicly resolvable but does not answer externally (egress verified via two live controls) — internal ELB in public DNS is an infra/banner observation, not an exposure.
