## STEP 6 — LEARNING

[LEARN] REJECTED AUTH @ mcp.sumup.com/mcp: JWT `alg:none` and RS256→HS256 key confusion are both explicitly refused by the **production** bearer verifier — `{"error":"invalid_token","error_description":"Unsupported \"alg\" value for a JSON Web Key Set"}` for both — and the allowlist is exactly `{RS256, EdDSA}` (RS384/RS512/PS256/ES256 → `no applicable key`). 29 cycles had never run the JWT-confusion class against a prod asset; it is now closed with a reproducible 6-value matrix rather than assumed. The surviving prod weakness is strictly narrower: `kid` is optional (RFC 8725 §3.11 try-all), which is a hardening deviation, not a bypass.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ mcp.sumup.com: RFC 9728 resource-server metadata is LIVE on the prod MCP host at two paths and publishes a `scopes_supported:["offline_access","email"]` model plus `resource_documentation: https://developer.sumup.com/tools/llms` — none of it in the KB, which had only probed the MCP app-directory file `/.well-known/mcp.json` and recorded its 404. A 404 on one `.well-known` path is not evidence the spec surface is absent.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED OATH @ auth.sumup.com: `client_id=dashboard` ACCEPTS `email` (302 `login_challenge`), completing its consent set as `{openid, classic, offline, readers.read, terminals.read, email}` while `offline_access` is rejected (303 `invalid_scope`) — the KB's "readers.read/terminals.read are the ONLY scopes" was a measurement gap, and `email` is precisely one of the two scopes the prod MCP server declares it needs.
[LEARN] REJECTED AUTH @ auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2-register/JWKS: a 30-candidate `kid` sweep against the prod MCP verifier found exactly the 8 published prod kids trusted and **0** undeclared — no stale, rotated-but-trusted, or rogue signing key in the prod trust store, and the staging `loadtesting` key is absent from prod. The key-lifecycle-drift hypothesis class is closed for this asset.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ auth.sam-app.ro JWKS: the staging trust set contains **2 duplicated entries** (`public:3a13954d-…`, `public:f06a4960-…` each twice) — 11 entries, 9 unique keys. Any kid-set size quoted from an entry count overstates the real key count and would corrupt a cross-environment overlap argument.

## STEP 7 — RISK

[RISK] sumup: 40. This cycle broke a 27-cycle no-delta streak with the first prod-side, non-banner, non-CORS observation the program has produced: a documented prod OAuth resource-server scope model (`mcp.sumup.com` RFC 9728), a newly measured scope in the stock `dashboard` client that satisfies half of it, and a 4-class prod kid/alg oracle. It also closed two long-open classes with evidence rather than assumption — JWT alg/key confusion on prod is explicitly refused, and the prod trust store contains no undeclared key. Residual risk is unchanged and dominated by credentials, not by surface: 3 of 4 surviving leads are AUTH_HELPED behind a merchant bearer, and the one complete PASSIVE deliverable (auth.sam-app.ro, VALID 7.5) is unsubmitted for the 15th cycle. No chainable exploit was achieved, so program risk stays low while discovery efficiency finally turns positive.
