[NEW] `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` **created and verified on disk** (410 lines, 18,590 B) — last cycle's `[NEXT]` directed a human to submit a file that did not exist, repeating the 8-cycle `contentful-preview-token-leak.md` hallucination. `reports/valid-bugs.md` extended to 114 lines with the finding and both analytical corrections.

[NEW] **`payment_type !== "card"` bypasses the frame-access gate entirely.** `if("card"===a.payment_type){ if(d=Ce(r.frames), !d.length) return; … }` — omit `payment_type` and `Ce()` is never called, `d` stays `[]`, and the payload's card object is taken verbatim from the attacker's message. The PoC needs no cooperating frames, so the only gate on the `PUT` is the UUID regex `le()`. This *raises* confidence in the main finding; prior notes implied the frame gate was a real barrier.

[NEW] **Exfiltration is blocked by an accident, not a control.** Three messengers are built from one `send`; only the container sets `origin: document.referrer`, and a full URL is an invalid `targetOrigin` so it throws. That is precisely the messenger carrying `form--on-result`. The two that *do* deliver use hardcoded `"*"` and carry only `{name}`, `{name,error,shouldShowError}` and the card brand — never PAN/CVV. Repairing `form--on-result` without adding `origin` validation would create a read primitive.

[NEW] **`js.sumup.com` — host absent from 30 cycles of inventory.** Live Vercel, `GET /` → 200/811 B "SumUp JS SDK" doc landing page. Referenced as `apiBFF: zi("https://js.sumup.com/api", sessionId)` in the parent SDK. All 5 other paths 404. Static, no dynamic surface.

[NEW] **`circuit.sumup.com` → 200/4,121 B** (logo origin, referenced from the new `js.sumup.com` page). `static.sumup.com` root 404 but serves `/favicons/*`.

[NEW] **`gateway.sumup.com` surface is now closed at 4 files + 1 asset family**: `/` (546 B), `/hosted.js` (26,839 B), `/sdk.js` (291,877 B), `/favicon.ico`, and `/gateway/ecom/card/v2/locales/{en,en-US}.json` (9,016 / 6,689 B, `access-control-allow-origin: *`) — a prefix my prior sweep missed because it only tried top-level paths. 15 other paths → uniform 79-byte 404; no `_next`, confirming static Vercel. Recorded so future cycles do not re-sweep.

[CHANGED] `hosted.js` re-verified byte-identical: sha256 `1302f1d6…f220873`, 26,839 B, so every code citation in the report is the code actually served. `Le` is `e=>!!e`, a null check — the `"WARNING: blocked access to frame"` log is a same-origin read failure, **not** a security control.

[CHANGED] **`X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id` is not a secret.** The first-party SDK derives it as `Ai(href)` → `checkout.sumup.com/pay/{id}` → `{origin:"Hosted Checkout", sessionId:<id>}`. It is the checkout id from the page URL, present in history/Referer/analytics/logs by design. This **downgrades** my own prior hypothesis #2 from 55/"High if reachable" — there is no privilege boundary to cross, so I am not carrying it forward at its old confidence.

