- 1 lead(s) marked VALID at 2026-09-26 16:46 UTC
  - **Verdict: VALID** — confidence 92, class MISCONFIG
  - **Asset:** `gateway.sumup.com` (`/`, `/hosted.js`) -> `api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{id}`
  - **Report file:** `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` — 198 lines, 8,532 B, sha256 `12bdc51a13b523110819d91fcaaf397a52c9672e2127ff13494cd7f5e854a3a8` (verified on disk this cycle)
  - **Defect:** `addEventListener("message",p)` destructures `{data:n,source:i}` only; `event.origin` is never read. Whole-bundle `grep -c 'event\.origin\|\.origin!==\|origin===\|\.origin=='` returns **0** across 26,839 served bytes (`/hosted.js` sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`, re-verified this cycle). No `X-Frame-Options`, no CSP `frame-ancestors`, no `Referrer-Policy` on `/` (`server: Vercel` only).
  - **Gate bypass:** the only structural barrier is conditional on a caller-supplied value — `if("card"===a.payment_type){if(d=Ce(r.frames),!d.length)return;` — so omitting `payment_type` skips `Ce()` entirely and the cooperating-frame requirement is never enforced.
  - **Attacker-controlled request:** `"X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id":r`, `headers["Sumup-Product-Origin"]=t.origin`, body `product_origin=i.origin` / `session_id=i.sessionId`, and the checkout id interpolated three times into `s.endpoint("checkouts/".concat(r),{method:"PUT",...})` — path, `X-Sumup-Correlation-Id`, and body. Cross-origin dispatch and the outbound `PUT` were captured live via netlog in a prior cycle.
  - **Sequencing hazard (report with the fix):** the response direction is blocked by a bug, not a control — the container messenger passes `origin: document.referrer` (a full URL) as `targetOrigin`, which throws, and it is the only messenger carrying `form--on-result`. Repairing that channel **without** adding `event.origin` validation converts this write primitive into a read primitive. Both must land in one change.
  - **Corrections to prior notes:** (a) the "UUID-shape regex" as the remaining gate did **not** reproduce on the current bundle and is NOT asserted in the report; (b) "widget-session replay" is withdrawn — the id is URL-borne (`checkout.sumup.com/pay/{id}`), not a secret, so disclosure crosses no privilege boundary.
  - **Honest limits:** not claimed that the request succeeds against a real checkout, and no exfiltration. Bounded by widget-session validity. Filed on the demonstrated cross-origin request primitive, not on clickjacking (out of scope).
  - **Fileability:** Q1 real YES. Q2 reachable YES. Q3 impact YES — any unauthenticated web origin, no merchant cooperation, makes a first-party `sumup.com` origin emit a state-changing request to the production payments API with attacker-chosen credential header, product origin and body (card, personal details incl. CPF, customer details, direct debit, mandate, installments, SCA mode); `input--initialize` also rewrites placeholder/type/autocomplete/maxLength/disabled on live PAN/CVV inputs. Bounded: Medium. Q4 provable non-invasively YES (static, GET-only, hash-pinned). Q5 novel YES.
  - **ACTION: HUMAN — submit `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` to bugs.olivermaicher.eu.**
EOF
