### 1. gateway.sumup.com hosted-fields cross-origin messenger — VALID, Medium

**Report file:** `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md`
**Verified on disk:** 310 lines, 12,533 B, sha256 `cd94b180fb2f3f45863d472c38a2978602a28eb4bc02e6f472fb33b121239a0f`

**Core facts (all re-verified this cycle from served bytes):**

- `GET /` and `GET /hosted.js` ship **no** `X-Frame-Options`, **no** `Content-Security-Policy`
  (hence no `frame-ancestors`), **no** `Referrer-Policy` — `grep -ic` returns **0** on both.
  The PCI card-entry frame is framable by any origin. Same-estate contrast:
  `payout-settings-edge.sumup.com` does set `x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN`.
- The `postMessage` handler is `addEventListener("message",p)` and destructures
  `{data, source}` only. `event.origin` is never read:
  `grep -c 'event\\.origin\\|\\.origin!==\\|origin===\\|\\.origin=='` over all 26,839 served
  bytes returns **0**. No allowlist exists.
- The only discriminator is a self-echo check plus `type === "SumUpCard"` — a constant in the
  attacker's own JSON, not a property of the sender.
- **The sole structural barrier is conditional on a caller-supplied value:**
  `if("card"===a.payment_type){if(d=Ce(r.frames),!d.length)return`. Set `payment_type` to
  anything but `"card"` and the frame-access check is never executed and the `return` never
  fires, so the request path is reached with zero cooperating frames.
- Reachable write: `s.endpoint("checkouts/".concat(r),{method:"PUT",headers:{"Content-Type":"application/json","X-Sumup-Correlation-Id":r},body:JSON.stringify(n)…})`
  with caller-set `X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id`, caller-set `Sumup-Product-Origin`, and an
  attacker-chosen body (card, personal details incl. CPF, customer details, direct debit,
  mandate, installments, SCA mode). `checkoutId` is read from `payment.checkoutId`, not
  top level.
- `input--initialize` additionally rewrites `placeholder`/`type`/`autocomplete`/`maxLength`/
  `disabled` on the live PAN and CVV inputs — UI-redress inside a PCI frame.
- **Bundle pin:** `/hosted.js` = 26,839 B, sha256
  `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`, `Last-Modified: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:17`.
  Every code citation in the report is the code actually served.

**Stated bounds (not claimed beyond these):** bounded by widget-session validity; the genuine
container `checkout.sumup.com/pay/{uuid}` is 403 (Vercel WAF) so it cannot itself be framed;
the SCA hop `3dsecure.sumup.com` is 403/118 B AWS-default, terminating the flow at the
checkout-write stage. **No response-exfiltration path is claimed.**

**Remediation-ordering hazard (must ship with the fix):** the outbound channel is closed by a
*bug*, not a control — the messenger passes `origin: document.referrer` (a full URL) as
`targetOrigin`, which throws on every call, and that is the only messenger carrying
`form--on-result`. Landing a fix to that broken channel *without* landing `event.origin`
