  reproduction, and an explicit statement of what is *not* claimed.

### #2 Q&A
- Q1 attacker reachable? **YES** — unauthenticated GET; app client IDs published in the 302.
- Q2 real impact? **PARTIAL** — deprecated grant enabled on two independent production clients and
  tokens would be delivered to the protected resource origin. Severity honestly capped at **Low**:
  the token origin serves no content (4/4 paths 302/0 B), so no same-origin reader of
  `location.hash` exists, and fragments never propagate via `Referer`. **No token leak claimed.**
- Q3 provable non-invasively? **YES** — controlled 5-value `response_type` matrix with a `bogus`
