## STEP 1 — DELTA

[NEW] `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` is **unauthenticated per-checkout resource resolution** with a controlled proof the credential is not load-bearing: the official SDK's `X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id` is injected unconditionally by `Bi` but its value is a verbatim regex capture of the path segment of `checkout.sumup.com/pay/{id}` (`Ai`), and a 3-way response control (with header / without header / with `?attempts=1`) is **byte-identical** at md5 `5e19511ce3b7d04787ca40001d2a7f03`. Reproducing the first-party call shape exactly grants nothing an anonymous `curl` did not already have.
[NEW] **Correction — BFF route table.** `/api/checkouts/{id}/apple-pay-session` returns the **84 B Vercel `text/plain` stub**, not an application class. Last cycle recorded it as a third response class. It is issued by `Di`/`Ei` against `api.sumup.com` v0.2 via `Fi`, not the BFF. The BFF has exactly **two** application routes: `GET checkouts/{id}` (181 B) and `POST checkouts/{id}/fee-calculation` (144 B). `/api/checkouts` and `/api/merchants/{uuid}` are stubs.
[NEW] `js.sumup.com/sdk.js` → **404** (79 B Vercel stub). `sdk.js` is served by `gateway.sumup.com` (291,877 B, sha256 `0fae546a…`). Recorded because the previous cycle's citation named the artifact without qualifying which host serves it.
[CHANGED] `checkoutId` shape gate: a **static literal** in `sdk.js` (`xi = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-…-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-…$/i`), superseding three cycles of "unrecoverable from served bytes". Material fact is new: the server applies **no** equivalent check — `AAAA-not-a-uuid` is looked up and reflected.
[CHANGED] `Ti` demo branch confirmed inert from source: `Ti=e=>Promise.resolve({demo:!0,message:"This is a demo…",payload:e})` — a local literal, never reaches the network. Not a finding; closed so it is not re-derived.
[CHANGED] `Referrer-Policy` absent from **all three** `gateway.sumup.com` responses (`/`, `/hosted.js`, `/sdk.js`) and not set in the frame document — on the one asset whose credential is a URL path segment.
