## STEP 1 — DELTA

[NEW] **The `origin` guard in `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` is applied in one direction only.** The messenger factory signature is `u=({id:e,fromWindow:r,toWindow:t,variant:a,origin:n,...})`, the container supplies it (`origin: document.referrer`), and its **sole** use is outbound: `if(t) return void t.postMessage(e, n||"*")`. The inbound handler is `p=r=>{const{data:n,source:i}=r;…}` — `event.origin` is never read. Grep over the 26,839 B bundle: `event.origin`=0, `origin===`=0, `origin!==`=0, `targetOrigin`=0. A developer reading this code sees origin scoping configured and concludes it is enforced; the direction that carries `form--submit` is the unguarded one.

[NEW] **The inbound guard set is fully enumerable and wholly attacker-controlled:** `data.type==="SumUpCard"`, `data.action==="message"`, `data.variant==="hostedfield"`, `data.message` truthy, plus a self-echo check on `event.source` vs stored `fromWindow`. All three constant values are published in the public bundle (`o=Object.freeze({TYPE:"SumUpCard",ACTION_MESSAGE:"message"})`, `variant:"hostedfield"`). No origin, no allowlist, no credential.

[NEW] **Correction with hard evidence — the checkoutId gate is a static literal in `hosted.js`:** `ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i`, `le=e=>ue.test(e)`. Three prior cycles cited a `new RegExp(a.pattern)` occurrence as proof the gate was a runtime pattern "unrecoverable from served bytes". That constructor is the **card-brand/IIN table** (`"pattern":"^((627416)|(637202)|(637200)|(637036)|(637201))","min":16,"max":16` — Visa/MC/AMEX IINs) — a different function. That claim is **retracted**.

[NEW] **BFF three-class control re-run live on `js.sumup.com/api`:** `checkouts/1111…5555` → 404/**181 B**/`application/json` (RFC 9457, id reflected); `checkouts/AAAA-not-a-uuid` → 404/**160 B**/`application/json` (id reflected, no server-side format check); `zzzz` → 404/**84 B**/`text/plain` (Vercel no-route stub). 181−160 = 21 B against a 20-character id-length difference — the response size tracks the reflected id, confirming reflection rather than a fixed template.

