## Objective
- Continue the SumUp bug-bounty hunt in POC phase and produce the required eight structured analysis blocks.
- Prioritize checkout IDOR/business-logic hypotheses while avoiding re-probing byte-stable surfaces.

## Important Details
- Live testing must remain passive-first, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 request/second, with no customer data, credentials, or mutating requests.
- Facts and hypotheses must be separated; drop confidence <40, rejected classes, and hypotheses without concrete verification steps.
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles; `reports/` artifacts do not persist reliably. Verify paths before relying on prior `[NEW]` claims.
- Leading API hypothesis: unauthenticated `GET https://api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` returns 58 B `{"error_code":"NOT_FOUND","message":"checkout not found"}`; malformed `Authorization` changes it to 500/0 B, proving credential parsing inside the handler.
- Endpoint is absent from the public OpenAPI spec, recovered from `gateway.sumup.com/sdk.js`; UUID validation exists client-side only. Disclosure impact remains unproven without a live checkout ID.
- Sibling hypothesis: `GET https://js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` returns an unauthenticated application-layer 404 with the identifier reflected; no valid-ID 200 has been obtained.
- Prior public SDK fixture ID may still be useful, but production checkout IDs are unlikely to exist in test fixtures.
- No live HTTP request has been made in the current cycle yet.

