## [FACTS — VERIFIED THIS CYCLE]
Base builder `Bi(host,session,origin,version)` → URL is `${host}/${version}/${path}`, injecting `X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id` and optional `Sumup-Product-Origin`. Complete graph = **6 operations**, confirming the KB count:

| Host | Op | Path |
|---|---|---|
| api.sumup.com | PUT | `/v0.2/checkouts/{id}` |
| api.sumup.com | PUT | `/v0.2/checkouts/{id}/apple-pay-session` |
| api.sumup.com | GET | `/v0.2/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` |
| api.sumup.com | POST | `/v0.1/internal/analytics` |
| js.sumup.com/api | GET | `/checkouts/{id}[?attempts=N]` |
| js.sumup.com/api | POST | `/checkouts/{id}/fee-calculation` |

- BFF facade `zi` is **closed at exactly 2 network ops**; all other members are React wiring (`children`, `events`, `trigger*`). No hidden BFF route exists.
- Client UUID gate: `^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i` — version `[0-5]`, variant `[089ab]`, enforced client-side only, before any request.
- `Ni()` = `["demo","demo-sandbox"].includes(id.toLowerCase().trim())`; on match `fetchByCheckout` returns a hardcoded card list with **zero network traffic** — proving the endpoint is only reached for genuine UUIDs.
- `attempts` is a client poll counter: `maxAttempts=60`, starts at 1, 5 s interval, halts when `status !== "PENDING"`.

Probes (all `cf-ray`/`x-vercel-id` distinct per request, so no cache artefact):

| Request | Result | Body hash |
|---|---|---|
| `/v0.2/checkouts/{uuid}/payment-methods` | 404, 58 B | `e296fc26` |
| `…?hosted_checkout=true` | 404, 58 B | `e296fc26` **identical** |
| `GET /api/checkouts/{uuid}` | 404, 181 B | `6725e39d` |
| `…?attempts=1` | 404, 181 B | `6725e39d` **identical** |
| `/v0.2/checkouts/demo/payment-methods` | 404, 58 B | `e296fc26` **identical** |
| `GET /api/checkouts/demo` | 404, 149 B | `c3273f7c` |

Quantitative result: the BFF body is `f(identifier)` — 181 B at 36 chars vs 149 B at 4 chars, a 32-byte delta for a 32-character delta. Exact linear correspondence ⇒ pure template substitution, **zero branching**.

## [HYPOTHESES — SEPARATED FROM FACTS]
- **H1 — api.sumup.com payment-methods unauth disclosure.** *Confidence reduced.* Every pre-existence discriminator is now exhausted and inert. The malformed-auth 500 remains the only evidence the credential is parsed inside the handler, and that does **not** establish that resource resolution happens after auth. Impact unproven.
- **H2 — BFF unauth checkout existence oracle.** *Confidence reduced.* The linear-substitution finding cuts both ways: it shows the app reaches its store and reflects the ID, but also that no pre-existence branch distinguishes live from dead checkouts, raising the bar for a bare 200.

Neither is fileable without a valid checkout ID.

