## Objective
- Continue the SumUp Group bug-bounty investigation in `POC` phase, target `api`, using passive/read-only evidence to validate or retire hypotheses and emit the required structured blocks.
- Immediate focus: complete the `js.sumup.com` BFF control, then assess the untested `pos-payment.sumup.com` route surface.

## Important Details
- Scope is SumUp-owned infrastructure, APIs, merchant/payment systems, and web applications only.
- Live testing must remain passive-first, read-only, ≤1 request/second, and limited to GET/HEAD/OPTIONS; no mutations, auth bypasses, or customer data.
- Required output blocks: `[DELTA]`, `[PRIO]`, up to three `[HYP]` entries, `[PARKED]`/`[FINAL]`, one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]`.
- `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` is application-routed, but an ID-reflecting 404 is not an existence oracle without a response differential.
- `api.sumup.com/v0.1/v0.2/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` is a scored tombstone: the latest 9 credential/identifier controls were byte-identical; do not reuse the stale confidence-92 ranking.
