## 2026-09-30 — cycle 38 (bigpickle)

**Running count: 1**

### Finding 1 — `gateway.sumup.com` hosted-fields: unguarded cross-origin `postMessage` inbound channel

- **Class:** MISCONFIG
- **Confidence:** 88
- **Severity:** Medium (bounded)
- **Evidence:** `hosted.js` 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`
- **Report:** `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` — 215 lines, sha256 `cf997909f114d86102124e9c2a9efb10c6f8ae6ed554366b3c703090ab314635`
- **Status:** VALID — FILE REPORT — **AWAITING HUMAN SUBMISSION**

The `origin` parameter is declared in the messenger factory signature and
supplied at the container construction site, but applied **only outbound**
(`t.postMessage(e, n || "*")` with `n = document.referrer`). The inbound
handler destructures `{data, source}` and never reads `event.origin`
(greps `event.origin` / `origin!==` / `origin===` = 0 / 0 / 0). No
`X-Frame-Options`, no `CSP frame-ancestors`, no `Referrer-Policy` on any of
`/`, `/hosted.js`, `/sdk.js`.

Bounded and explicitly NOT claimed: response exfiltration (outbound payloads
carry only data the sender already knew); widget-session replay (`X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id`
is a URL-borne identifier from `checkout.sumup.com/pay/{id}`, not a secret);
the PUT is not a faithful merchant replay (arrives without `product_origin`/
`session_id`); and no chain to `js.sumup.com` (`grep -c 'js\.sumup\.com' hosted.js` = 0).

| Q | A |
|---|---|
| Q1 Attacker reachable? | **YES** — `payment_type !== "card"` skips the frame-access gate entirely; a cross-origin `form--submit` drives `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{id}`. |
| Q2 Authentication required? | **NO** — no origin, identity, or frame-registration check on inbound. |
| Q3 Impact if exploited? | **Bounded** — state-changing API call with attacker-chosen payload; API acceptance unproven; no exfiltration path exists as implemented. |
| Q4 Provable non-invasively? | **YES** — proven via netlog + iframe console, read-only observation of an outbound request. |
| Q5 Novel / unreported? | **Likely** — not previously in this ledger. |

