## Objective
- Continue the SumUp bug-bounty POC cycle for `api` and emit only the required 8-step structured analyst blocks.

## Important Details
- Current state: `phase=POC`, `target=api`.
- Enforce passive-first rules: live probes only `GET`/`HEAD`/`OPTIONS`, ≤1 rps, no customer-data mutation, no scanner-only findings, and no out-of-scope classes.
- No submission mechanism exists locally: `scope.yml:4` names `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`; `scripts/sync-issues.py` and `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` only mirror leads to GitHub.
- Workspace is repeatedly re-materialized between cycles; verify every report with `ls`, `wc`, and `sha256sum` before referencing it.
- Leading finding: `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js`, confidence 88, Medium. Cross-origin frame has no inbound `event.origin` check or framing headers and emits attacker-shaped `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{uuid}`. API acceptance is unproven and `HUMAN_ONLY`.
- `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js`: 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`.
- Comparative control: `payout-settings-edge.sumup.com` returns `x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN`; `gateway.sumup.com` returns no `X-Frame-Options`, CSP `frame-ancestors`, or `Referrer-Policy`.
- Gateway report was independently re-audited with 10/10 reproducible claims; latest measurement was 167 lines, 8,951 B, sha256 `91d95c0f1dcb6943b6727f32b53fb6596a27c8aa365cb86bd41a0cd4011979ce`.
- Secondary finding: `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` permits unauthenticated RFC 7591 registration and mints empty-scope JWTs; redirect allowlist, PKCE, and cross-environment JWKS isolation bound impact. Confidence 72, human-only, unsubmitted.
- `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` is parked at 5: 5 identifiers × 7 credential shapes produced identical 404/58 B responses; the former 92-confidence credential differential was transient.
- `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` existence-oracle claim is refuted; current response is the 68 B Vercel platform 404.
- `serial-terminal.dev.solo.sumup.com` gate inconsistency remains confidence 50 with exposure unproven; `iso20022.sumup.com` routing is confidence 45 with no demonstrated security impact.
- Current risk score: 80. Discovery yield is low; delivery is the main remaining risk.

## Work State
### Completed
- Re-verified and independently reproduced all 10 gateway report claims.
- Added a per-claim reproduction table and verified the `window.parent` initialization plus comparative framing control.
- Tombstoned the former 92-confidence payment-methods lead with its full 35-response negative matrix.
- Confirmed no automated private-program submission path exists.
- Closed stale Contentful-preview-token work: credential rotated and finding non-reproducible.
- Closed prod MCP `alg:none`/HS256 confusion; prod allows only `{RS256, EdDSA}`.

### Active
- Gateway report is evidence-complete but awaiting manual submission to `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- `auth.sam-app.ro` dynamic-registration finding remains a secondary unsubmitted human-only item.
- Workspace persistence must be checked before relying on any prior artifact.

### Blocked
- Manual private-program submission cannot be performed from the repository.
- Whether `api.sumup.com` accepts the gateway-emitted checkout PUT requires a mutating customer-data test and is out of bounds.
- Report artifacts may disappear because the workspace re-materializes between cycles.

## Next Move
