## Objective
- Continue the SumUp bug-bounty hunt from phase `POC` targeting `api`, producing only the requested 8-step structured blocks.
- Prioritize evidence-complete money/auth logic flaws, reject stale leads, and prepare human-submittable findings.

## Important Details
- Scope: SumUp-owned assets only; report through `https://bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live probing is passive-first, `<=1 rps`, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only unless explicitly `AUTH_HELPED`; no mutating tests against customer data.
- Output schema and rules: one `[NEW]`/`[CHANGED]` per line, three scored `[PRIO]`, at most three strict-schema `[HYP]`, self-critique, exactly one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]`.
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles; prior file claims are not ground truth. Always start with `ls`, then verify newly written files with `wc` and `sha256sum`.
- Leading finding: `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` lacks inbound `event.origin` validation and framing protections; cross-origin `form--submit` generated `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{id}`. Server-side acceptance remains unproven, so impact is capped at Medium.
- Current live bundle: `https://gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js`, 26,839 B, SHA-256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`.
- DCR lead: `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` is live and mints JWTs, but observed `scp=[]`; attacker-controlled `aud` does not imply production relay because prod/staging JWKS key sets do not overlap.
- Do not revive retired API/IDOR claims: 35 checkout-payment-methods responses were byte-identical; the lone `500/0 B` was transient.
- `iso20022.sumup.com` ELB/Istio routing divergence is recon only—no protected route, data, or authz bypass was shown.
- Contentful Preview token finding is closed: token rotated to 401 and `reports/contentful-preview-token-leak.md` remains absent.

