  - | Frame-access gate bypass | The cooperating-frame check `Ce(r.frames)` sits inside `if("card"===a.payment_type){…}` and early-returns on empty. Omit `payment_type` and it never runs — a conditional guard a caller-supplied discriminator can skip is not a guard. |
  - | checkoutId gate (CORRECTED) | Three earlier cycles got this wrong three different ways (bare "unrecoverable runtime pattern" → full retraction → "static literal in another file"). Served code settles it: `return qe(r)?Ee(n):le(r)?(a&&(n.sca_e…))…:pe(r)`, `le=e=>ue.test(e)`, `pe=e=>Promise.reject(new Error("Invalid UUID checkout: ".concat(e)))`. `ue` is a **static literal**, verbatim in `hosted.js` and again in `sdk.js` as `xi`: `/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i`. Gate IS load-bearing and IS fully recovered — but it protects nothing, because **the attacker chooses `checkoutId`**. A shape check on attacker-controlled input is a client-side sanity check, not an authorisation boundary. |
  - | Widget-session credential | `Te.endpoint` sets `{"X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id": r}` **unconditionally** → literal string `"undefined"` when absent. Only `Sumup-Product-Origin` is conditional. First-party SDK derives it from `checkout.sumup.com/pay/{id}` (a URL path segment) via host-pinned extractor `fe` (`r.host==="checkout.sumup.com"`, `/pay/([^?/#]+)`), which returns nothing on `gateway.sumup.com`. Structurally void credential with attacker-chosen value; `"Session id" in a header name is not evidence the value is a secret`. |
  - | Q4 Provable non-invasively? | **PARTIAL** — every code-level claim is re-derivable offline from the served bundle; the browser-level PoC that the frame emits the PUT requires a merchant page to embed the frame. No customer data needed. |
  - | Q5 Novel/unreported? | **YES** — not in `valid-bugs.md` as a filed report in any prior block; no gateway host appears in any prior VALID entry. |
  - | Q6 In-scope? | YES — company-owned payment platform; card-entry frame is PCI-scoped surface. **NOT** reported as bare clickjacking (explicitly out of scope); the claim is the demonstrated cross-origin message-driven write. |
  - | Q7 Reasonable triager? | YES for Medium — missing origin validation on a frame that exists to be third-party-framed, driving a payment write, with the one fix (`targetOrigin` on outbound) already present-but-misapplied in the same file. Needs the merchant throwaway test to consider High. |
  - | Severity | **6.5 / 10 (Medium)** — capped by unproven server-side acceptance; High only if the PUT lands. |
  - | Confidence | HIGH on every code claim (all re-extracted from served bytes this cycle; 18-row per-claim reproduction table in the report). |
  - | DELIBERATELY NOT CLAIMED | (a) `js.sumup.com` BFF chain — `grep -c 'js\.sumup\.com' hosted.js` = **0** vs `grep -c '"https://api\.sumup\.com"'` = 1; a two-finding cross-origin money chain was proposed and **killed by that grep**. (b) demo/sandbox exposure — `qe=e=>[he,_e].includes(e)`, `he="demo"`, `_e="demo-sandbox"`, and `Ee=e=>Promise.resolve({demo:!0,message:"This is a demo. Not a real checkout is processed."…})` is a local literal that never touches the network. (c) response exfiltration — two messengers do have a working wildcard outbound (`e.postMessage(t,"*")`), so the channel is open, but the payloads (`aux--metric-track--ack`; an `input--blur` field name the attacker chose and already knows) are values the sender already held. **A finding needs a capability differential; there is none in the content that flows.** |
  - | Sequencing risk for the fix | `n = document.referrer` is a **full URL** passed as `targetOrigin`, which throws — a bug, not a control — and `n\|\|"*"` means an **empty referrer selects the wildcard**. Landing the outbound fix alone puts `origin` to more correct-looking use while inbound stays open; land both together. |
  - | Action | **FILE REPORT** → `https://bugs.olivermaicher.eu` (no submission mechanism in repo — human submission required). Report: `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md`, 211 lines, 11,781 B, sha256 `19c620133e36250e0da2c5bac8172385c7c49a75e8f3cc26feda5ce38efdf0f1` |
