   - | Misleading evidence | The messenger factory is `u=({id:e,fromWindow:r,toWindow:t,variant:a,origin:n,…})`. `origin` is a declared param, supplied at the construction site, and applied on exactly ONE path — the **outbound** send (`if(t)return void t.postMessage(e,n\|\|"*")`). A reviewer finds `origin` in scope, sees it used, and concludes inbound is covered. **A credential argument being present is not evidence it is enforced.** |
   - | Q3 Real impact? | PARTIAL — cross-origin message channel drives `PUT https://api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{attacker-id}` from inside the SumUp hosted-fields frame: `.endpoint("checkouts/".concat(r),{method:"PUT",…,"X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id":r,…})`, base `("https://api.sumup.com",n,s)`. **Emission proven; server-side acceptance unproven** — that leg needs a merchant-authorised throwaway checkout. |
   - | Frame-access gate bypass | The cooperating-frame check `Ce(r.frames)` sits inside `if("card"===a.payment_type){…}` and early-returns on empty. Omit `payment_type` and it never runs — a conditional guard a caller-supplied discriminator can skip is not a guard. |
   - | checkoutId gate (CORRECTED) | Three earlier cycles got this wrong three different ways (bare "unrecoverable runtime pattern" → full retraction → "static literal in another file"). Served code settles it: `return qe(r)?Ee(n):le(r)?(a&&(n.sca_e…))…:pe(r)`, `le=e=>ue.test(e)`, `pe=e=>Promise.reject(new Error("Invalid UUID checkout: ".concat(e)))`. `ue` is a **static literal**, verbatim in `hosted.js` and again in `sdk.js` as `xi`: `/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i`. Gate IS load-bearing and IS fully recovered — but it protects nothing, because **the attacker chooses `checkoutId`**. A shape check on attacker-controlled input is a client-side sanity check, not an authorisation boundary. |

