Rebuilt the report with a verifiable sidecar digest and appended the ledger entry. Both artifacts now survive with proven integrity.

**What I did this cycle:**

Killed a lead cheaply — `js.sumup.com/` is a zero-JS static page with no script tags, so the "recover call shapes from js.sumup.com's chunks" idea died in one request.

Then found a real error in my own records. My 2026-09-30 note said `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` was "refuted, 68B Vercel platform 404." That's a misattribution: the 84B `text/plain` stub I remembered belongs to a *different* endpoint's nonsense-path control. The actual `/api/checkouts/{uuid}` returns 181B `application/json` RFC-9457, byte-stable across repeats, with `Checkout … does not exist` reflected verbatim. The route is application-routed. The credential being void (6/6 shapes, md5 `5e19511c`) was the 09-27 finding and stands — but the route-existence part of the refutation was wrong.

Re-verified the gateway artifact from served bytes rather than trusting prior notes: `hosted.js` sha256 `1302f1d6…`, six origin-validation greps at 0, and `GET /` returns zero framing headers.

**Two corrections I made to my own process:**

I had a report self-hash embedded in the report. That can't work — writing the digest mutates the bytes it describes, so the recorded value was wrong the moment it landed. Moved it to a `.sha256` sidecar that `sha256sum -c` verifies.

My first credential-differential loop was broken shell quoting (`curl: (6) Could not resolve host: Bearer`). Those errors were my bug, not results. Re-ran properly before drawing any conclusion.

**Current state:** report 216 lines / 8970 B, digest verified; `valid-bugs.md` 93 lines with the gateway entry appended (backup at `.bak.79`).

**The one thing blocking High severity is server-side acceptance of the emitted PUT.** That needs a real merchant session and a throwaway checkout, which I can't do passively. Everything else in the report is evidence-complete from static analysis.

One caveat worth flagging: the report is unsubmitted. There's no submission mechanism in this repo — `scripts/sync-issues.py` mirrors leads into GitHub issues, and it won't reach `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`. That step is yours.

Want me to commit these artifacts, or leave them uncommitted so you can review the report text before submitting?
