## Objective
- Continue the SumUp bug-bounty hunt, validate only in-scope logic/security flaws, and produce the requested STEP 1–7 structured output.
- Current phase: `POC`; target: `api`.

## Important Details
- Live testing is passive-first: read-only `GET`/`HEAD`/`OPTIONS`, ≤1 rps; no mutation against live customer data.
- Report channel: `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`; no local submission mechanism exists.
- Workspace is repeatedly re-materialized between cycles. Always open with `ls`; write and hash files in the same command before claiming they exist.
- Current gateway evidence: `https://gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js`, 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`.
- Gateway inbound `postMessage` handler does not validate `event.origin`; framing headers are absent. Cross-origin `form--submit` reaches `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{id}`. Server acceptance remains unproven.
- `auth.sam-app.ro` exposes RFC 7591 registration and mints JWTs, but observed `scp` is empty. Prod/staging JWKS have zero `kid` overlap; staging has 11 entries but only 9 unique keys. Prod-relay impact is unsupported.
- `iso20022.sumup.com` has an ELB-before-Istio boundary: raw paths containing case-sensitive `metrics` return fixed `503`; others return `400`. No attacker capability or security impact is demonstrated.
- Retired: `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR, `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` BFF oracle, `pos-payment.sumup.com` route enumeration, MCP JWT algorithm confusion, and Contentful preview-token leak.

## Work State
### Completed
- Reconstructed `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md`: last measured 190 lines, 8,722 B, sha256 `2fb3f7dcc8bcae7d24f846262b1617f21db8fc44c49ab061426a987d45a11737`.
- Corrected the report’s mistyped `hosted.js` hash before writing.
- Updated `reports/valid-bugs.md`: last measured 160 lines, 13,994 B, sha256 `9aacaba0e21d7e4a9df08388e617d7cab02e92f2c2ae87732a7737bbfafee7a2`.
- Confirmed `mcp.sumup.com/mcp` GET requires bearer auth; third RFC 9728 document is live at `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp`.
- Confirmed staging advertises `registration_endpoint`; production omits it.
- Closed `serial-terminal.dev.solo.sumup.com` as a client-only Web Serial PWA with no remote API, token, or exploitable data exposure.

### Active
- Gateway hosted-fields finding ranked first; only server-side acceptance on a throwaway checkout separates Medium from High.
- Staging DCR scope-gap remains the second-ranked hypothesis; needs an authorized token response with non-empty `scp` to raise severity.
- ISO 20022 ELB/Istio routing boundary remains recon-only pending an actual capability differential.

### Blocked
- Gateway server acceptance requires `HUMAN_ONLY` testing with a throwaway checkout.
- DCR scope escalation requires `AUTH_HELPED` credentials/flow.
- Report files may disappear after re-materialization; last hashes are not durable evidence.
- Human submission is required; `scripts/sync-issues.py` and `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` only mirror leads.

