## Objective
- Continue the authorized SumUp bug-bounty hunt in `POC` phase for `api`, prioritizing money/auth logic while avoiding stale re-probes and unsupported claims.

## Important Details
- Scope: SumUp-owned infrastructure and applications; exclude DoS, TLS hygiene, descriptive headers, public files, scanner-only findings, clickjacking without impact, and other listed out-of-scope classes.
- Live probes must be passive-first, `GET`/`HEAD`/`OPTIONS` only, `<=1 rps`; no mutating requests against customer data.
- Required output is exactly the eight structured blocks: `DELTA`, `PRIORITIZE`, `HYPOTHESES`, `SELF-CRITIQUE`, `NEXT ACTION`, `LEARNING`, `RISK`.
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles. Start with `ls`; never trust a prior `[NEW]` file claim. Write and hash in one command before referencing an artifact.
- Submission is manual at `https://bugs.olivermaicher.eu`; `scripts/sync-issues.py` and `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` mirror leads only.
- Gateway finding: `https://gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` is 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`; inbound handler never reads `event.origin`, and `/` has no `X-Frame-Options`/CSP `frame-ancestors`.
- Gateway cross-origin `form--submit` has emitted `PUT https://api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{id}`; server-side acceptance remains the missing proof, so severity is capped at Medium.
- `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` is unauthenticated and advertises 19 scopes, but minted JWTs currently have `scp:[]`; prod/staging JWKS have zero overlap, blocking any unsupported prod-relay claim.
- `iso20022.sumup.com` routing is recon only: raw paths containing case-sensitive `metrics` reach `awselb/2.0` 503; other paths reach Istio 400. No data/authz bypass is demonstrated.
- Retired: `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR—35 identifier/credential responses were invariant; the lone 500 was transient.
- Retired: Contentful preview-token leak—credential rotated to 401; `mcp.sumup.com` CORS, JWT confusion, dashboard redirect widening, serial-terminal exposure, and `js.sumup.com` checkout oracle are also closed/non-fileable.

