## Objective
- Continue SumUp bug-bounty hunting in `POC` for `api`, rank current surfaces, and produce only evidence-backed hypotheses under passive/read-only rules.
- Advance the hosted-fields cross-origin messenger finding without overstating unproven server-side impact.

## Important Details
- Scope: SumUp-owned infrastructure and applications; report via `https://bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live probing: ≤1 rps, passive-first, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; no mutating tests against customer data.
- Workspace re-materializes between cycles: start with `ls`; treat prior file claims as untrusted; write and hash reports in the same command.
- Current ranking:
  1. `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` — confidence 88, `HUMAN_ONLY`.
  2. `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` — confidence 62, `AUTH_HELPED`.
  3. `iso20022.sumup.com` routing boundary — confidence 42, `PASSIVE`.
- Gateway fact: `/hosted.js` is 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`; inbound handler never reads `event.origin`, framing headers are absent, and cross-origin `form--submit` emits `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{uuid}`.
- Gateway limits: emitted credentials may be absent/void (`X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id: "undefined"`), response exfiltration was not demonstrated, and server acceptance remains unproven; cap at Medium until tested with a throwaway checkout.
- Staging DCR: unauthenticated registration mints JWTs with empty `scp`; advertised scopes are not granted. Prod/staging metadata differ only by `registration_endpoint`; JWKS overlap is zero, so a production-relay claim is unsupported.
- `api.sumup.com` passive surface is exhausted; retire the prior `v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR and `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` oracle claims.
