## Work State
### Completed
- Verified `https://gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` is 26,839 B with sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`.
- Proved the frame lacks `X-Frame-Options`, CSP `frame-ancestors`, and `Referrer-Policy`.
- Proved inbound `postMessage` handling never reads `event.origin`; `origin` is used only in outbound `t.postMessage(e,n||"*")`.
- Proved `payment_type !== "card"` skips the cooperating-frame gate and permits `form--submit` to cause `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{attacker-chosen-uuid}`.
- Confirmed the checkout ID gate is the static UUID v1–v5 literal `/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i`.
- Read emission code at source: attacker-origin requests structurally lack `product_origin` and `session_id`; API success and resulting payment/checkout state remain unproven. No response-exfiltration capability is established.
- Retired the 92-confidence `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR after 35 responses were identifier- and credential-invariant; the earlier invalid-token `500/0 B` was transient.
- Refuted the `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` BFF oracle: it is a 68 B Vercel platform 404 and four credential controls were identical.
- Confirmed staging DCR at `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register`; tokens have empty `scp`, production lacks registration, and prod/staging JWKS have zero key overlap.
- Confirmed prod MCP JWT confusion is blocked: `{RS256,EdDSA}` only; `none`/HS256 rejected. Optional `kid` is hardening-only.
- Mapped `iso20022.sumup.com` routing as a case-sensitive `metrics` substring split, but rejected it as a vulnerability because no capability differential exists.
- Corrected Contentful Preview token status: credential rotated with HTTP 401; finding closed and must not be revived.

