## Objective
- Continue the SumUp bug-bounty POC/recon cycle, prioritizing defensible findings and producing only the required eight structured blocks.
- Deliver the strongest gateway and staging OAuth findings without reviving rejected hypotheses or claiming unsubmitted work as filed.

## Important Details
- State: `phase=POC`, `target=api`. Scope is SumUp-owned infrastructure; disclosure channel is `https://bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live testing is passive-first, `<=1 rps`, using GET/HEAD/OPTIONS; no mutating customer-data tests, DoS, auth bypass, TLS findings, scanner-only claims, or clickjacking without demonstrated impact.
- The workspace is repeatedly re-materialized between cycles. Always open with `ls`; write and hash artifacts in the same command before referencing them.
- Leading finding: `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` accepts cross-origin `postMessage` without reading `event.origin` and has no framing headers. A PoC emitted `PUT https://api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555`.
- Gateway evidence: `/hosted.js` is 26,839 B, SHA-256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`; inbound handler reads `{data,source}`, while `origin` is used only outbound as `t.postMessage(e, n||"*")`.
- Gateway impact must stay narrow: state-changing request emission is proven, but API acceptance and checkout modification are unproven. `product_origin`/`session_id` are absent in attacker-origin requests; no response-exfiltration primitive is established. Severity is capped at Medium pending sandbox validation.
- `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` permits unauthenticated RFC 7591 registration and `client_credentials` token minting with empty `scp`; scope/resource access and production relay are blocked. File only as a staging posture issue.
- Workspace has no submission mechanism: `scope.yml:4` names the private program, while `scripts/sync-issues.py` and `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` only synchronize leads.
- Closed/rejected leads: `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR retired after 35 invariant responses; `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` is a Vercel 404 reflector; `pos-payment.sumup.com` has no route discriminator; `iso20022.sumup.com` dual routing is recon-only; MCP JWT confusion and permissive CORS classes are rejected.

