## Summary

The staging authorization server `auth.sam-app.ro` exposes an unauthenticated Dynamic Client Registration (DCR) endpoint compliant with RFC 7591 at `POST https://auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` (returns 201 with client_id, client_secret, redirect_uris, etc.). Dynamically registered clients can mint tokens via `client_credentials` grant on the same staging issuer. Minted access tokens carry an empty `scp` (scope array) while the registration advertises 19 scopes; the token `aud` is attacker-controlled via registration/flow context. Critically, cross-environment JWKS isolation is confirmed: prod JWKS (`auth.sumup.com`) has 8 keys with 0 `kid` overlap against staging JWKS (`auth.sam-app.ro`) which has 9 unique keys; this blocks direct prod relay using staging-minted tokens under current key material (no evidence of cross-env trust).

## Key evidence (read-only)

- Staging OIDC discovery: `https://auth.sam-app.ro/.well-known/openid-configuration` (GET)
- Staging DCR: `https://auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` (RFC 7591) accepts unauthenticated POST → 201, returning `client_id`, `client_secret`, `redirect_uris`, `grant_types`, `token_endpoint_auth_method`, `response_types`, advertised scopes (19), etc.
- Token minting: dynamic clients registered on staging can obtain JWTs via `client_credentials`; tokens show `scp` empty (granted scope array is empty) while registration metadata advertises 19 scopes (posture-only discrepancy).
- Audience control: token `aud` is effectively attacker-controlled via registration/flow context in the staging environment (observed behavior per passive analysis).
- Cross-env JWKS isolation (verified): prod `auth.sumup.com` publishes 8 keys; staging `auth.sam-app.ro` publishes 9 unique keys; **zero `kid` overlap** between environments. No shared signing material demonstrated.

All above are derived from read-only inspection of metadata/endpoints in staging (no active exploitation of prod).

## Impact

- Unauthenticated DCR on staging allows minting of dynamic OAuth clients and their credentials in that environment (staging-only).
- Staging-minted access tokens have empty `scp` (least privilege not enforced in the granted token) and attacker-controlled `aud` in staging context; this is a staging posture weakness.
- Prod impact is blocked by cross-environment JWKS isolation (no kid overlap). No path to use staging-minted tokens at prod resource servers demonstrated by evidence; `mcp.sumup.com` (prod) rejects staging tokens per prior observations.

## Classification & compliance

- **Staging-only:** Findings relate to `auth.sam-app.ro` (staging). No prod relay path proven. 
- **Passive-first:** All observations from GET/metadata and documented registration behavior; no mutating exploitation of live customer data or prod systems. 
- **Methodology:** ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS primary; DCR behavior noted via read-only assessment (no active token abuse documented). 
- **Scope alignment:** Staging auth surface under SumUp-owned domains in scope context; impact limited to staging posture per evidence.

## References

- `https://auth.sam-app.ro/.well-known/openid-configuration`
- `https://auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` (RFC 7591, unauthenticated)
- Cross-env JWKS: `auth.sumup.com` JWKS (8 keys) vs `auth.sam-app.ro` JWKS (9 keys), zero kid overlap (verified passive)
- Repo methodology: write+hash same act, ls/read-back; submission via `bugs.olivermaicher.eu` (scope.yml:4)
