## Objective
- Continue the scoped bug bounty hunt against SumUp Payments Limited / SumUp Group assets (per `scope.yml`, report channel: `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`) with a focus on high-value logic/auth flaws. 
- Maintain a passive-first, evidence-driven workflow (<=1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only for live probes), strictly separate facts from hypotheses, and avoid mutating tests against live customer data.

## Important Details
- **Scope**: Only company-owned infrastructure, payment platforms, merchant portals, APIs, mobile/web apps, POS, cloud services, websites and domains operated by SumUp Group and its subsidiaries. Out-of-scope classes (e.g. DoS, rate-limit, TLS best practice, self-XSS, username enumeration, etc.) are to be REJECTED.
- **Workspace persistence**: The workspace is re-materialized between cycles (artifacts written in cycle N do not persist to N+1). Any `[NEW]` file claim must be written and verified (`ls`, `wc -l`, `sha256sum`, `head`/`tail`) in the same command before being referenced. Treat any claim without an in-context hash as unproven.
- **Submission blocker**: No submission mechanism exists in the repo (`scope.yml:4` -> `bugs.olivermaicher.eu` private program). `scripts/sync-issues.py` and `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` only mirror leads. Deliverables must be submitted manually by a HUMAN.
- **Current lead (highest confidence)**: `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` cross-origin postMessage checkout-write (confidence 90). 
  - File: `https://gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` (26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`, etag `28e75d6c`, Vercel, ACAO `*`)
  - Missing `event.origin` validation on inbound postMessage (handler never reads `event.origin`); framable with no `X-Frame-Options`/`CSP frame-ancestors`/`Referrer-Policy` on `/`, `/hosted.js`, `/sdk.js`.
  - `checkoutId` gate is a static UUID v1–5 literal (`ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i`, `le=e=>ue.test(e)`) built at runtime but pattern is recoverable; `payment_type !== "card"` branch skips the frame-access gate entirely.
  - Outbound: three messenger sites — `Re` (container) sets `origin: document.referrer` (full URL) which throws on send, `Ue` (metrics) and `M` use literal `"*"` (wildcard outbound live). `X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id` is a checkout id (URL-derived), not a secret.
- **Second lead**: `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` — unauthenticated RFC 7591 dynamic client registration (confidence 85, staging-only). POST → 201 with client_id+secret+chosen redirect_uris; mints JWTs via `client_secret_post` (empty `scp`, attacker-controlled `aud`), but cross-env JWKS isolation holds (prod 8 keys, staging 9 unique, ZERO kid overlap); prod has no `/register` endpoint (`404 GET/POST/OPTIONS` on `auth.sumup.com`).
- **Retired/refuted this cycle**: `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` BFF existence-oracle (refuted — 4/4 credential differential checks failed, 68B Vercel platform 404), `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR (refuted — credential-invariant 58B `{"error_code":"NOT_FOUND"}` stub), `pos-payment.sumup.com` route-level enum (refuted by negative control).
- **Passive surface state**: `api.sumup.com` quartet is byte-stable (27+ consecutive cycles) — `v0.1/merchants/{code}/payment-methods` now 404 unauthenticated (gateway requires bearer even for spec-declared `oauth2:[]`), RFC 9728 metadata static (200), apple-pay GET structured 404, prod JWKS 8-kid. `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` GET 404 (POST-only). Re-probing these is zero-yield waste.

