[HYPOTHESIS]
- **H1 — accepted (confidence 90, Medium).** `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` mounts its messenger with `addEventListener("message", p)` and no origin filter; `event.origin` occurs 0 times in the bundle. The `origin` value is declared and passed into the factory yet consumed only by outbound `send`/`sendTo`, which use `"*"` and `n||"*"`. The shell carries no `X-Frame-Options` and no `frame-ancestors`. When `payment_type !== "card"`, the frame-origin gate is skipped entirely and control reaches `s.endpoint("checkouts/".concat(r),{method:"PUT",…})` with an attacker-supplied path segment and body; only a static, publicly readable UUID v1–5 regex remains. Live netlog confirms the `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{attacker-chosen-id}` is emitted. Bounded and explicitly not claimed: downstream payment acceptance (widget-session/backend validity), response exfiltration, and any card-data read. Same defect class present in `sdk.js` (`0fae546a…`), so remediation should be systematic.
- **H2 — accepted (confidence 85, Low-Medium, staging only).** `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` returns `201` with `client_id`/`client_secret` to an unauthenticated caller, accepts attacker-chosen `redirect_uris`, and mints JWTs via `client_credentials` + `client_secret_post` with empty `scp` and attacker-controlled `aud`. The staging gateway validates the token (structured `problem+json` 404 vs plain 404 without). Genuine controls bound it: scope escalation blocked at registration, PKCE required, per-client `redirect_uri` allowlist holds (`401` otherwise), no RFC 7592 management endpoints, prod `/register` is `404`, and cross-env `kid` overlap is zero. Prod client-provenance sync is untested and reported as such.
- **H3 — parked (confidence 75, informational).** `mcp.sumup.com/mcp` distinguishes four unauthenticated verifier error classes, including "multiple matching keys" when `kid` is omitted (RFC 8725 §3.11 try-all). Alg allowlist is exactly `{RS256, EdDSA}`. Hardening deviation only — no key confusion, no alg confusion, no untrusted keys in the trust store, no cross-env reuse. Not fileable without a practical exploit path.

[NEXT]
Human-only step: file both verified reports to `https://bugs.olivermaicher.eu` per `scope.yml:4`. No automated path exists in-repo — `scripts/sync-issues.py` and `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` mirror leads, not reports. Both report texts are final and self-contained, so the submitter needs no prior context. No further live probing is warranted: the gateway PoC is proven and mutating, DCR is proven and mutating, and the remaining API authorization question is unresolvable without a valid merchant bearer.
