## Objective
- Finalize and submit two SumUp bug-bounty reports covering the hosted-fields cross-origin checkout-write flaw and staging unauthenticated dynamic client registration.

## Important Details
- Follow passive-first testing: live probes limited to GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, ≤1 rps; do not repeat mutating registration/token/PoC requests without authorization.
- Scope is limited to SumUp-owned assets; clickjacking without demonstrated exploit, descriptive headers, TLS hygiene, OPTIONS-only observations, and unvalidated scanner findings are rejected classes.
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles; artifacts written in one cycle may disappear in the next.
- At cycle start, run `ls`; never trust a prior report-path claim without direct verification.
- If reconstructing a report, perform the write and `ls`/`wc`/`sha256sum` verification in the same command.
- Primary gateway finding: `https://gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js`, 26,839 B, SHA-256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`.
- Gateway evidence: no `event.origin` validation; no `X-Frame-Options` or CSP `frame-ancestors`; cross-origin `form--submit` issues `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{uuid}`. Request issuance is proven; full payment acceptance remains `AUTH_HELPED`.
- Gateway gates: `payment_type !== "card"` skips the cooperating-frame check; checkout ID uses static UUID v1–v5 regex `/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i`.
- Gateway remediation must move/apply origin validation inbound and fix outbound `postMessage` target handling together; wildcard outbound sites exist, but no sensitive-response exfiltration capability is currently demonstrated.
- Staging DCR: unauthenticated `POST https://auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` returns `201`; client credentials can mint JWTs with empty `scp` and attacker-controlled `aud`.
- DCR is staging-only: empty scope blocks resource access; production `/oauth2/register` is absent and prod/staging JWKS keys have zero overlap. Staging has 11 entries but 9 unique keys; production has 8.
- Production client-provenance synchronization remains explicitly untested; do not claim it is closed.
- `mcp.sumup.com/mcp` kid-optional try-all is parked hardening only; `alg:none` and RS256→HS256 confusion are rejected, with allowlist `{RS256, EdDSA}`.

