## Important Details
- Scope only SumUp-owned infrastructure; reject TLS findings, clickjacking without exploit, scanner-only reports, descriptive errors/headers, and other listed out-of-scope classes.
- Live probes must remain passive-first: `GET`/`HEAD`/`OPTIONS`, `<=1 rps`; no mutating requests or live customer data.
- Required output is only the eight structured blocks: `[NEW]/[CHANGED]`, `[PRRIO]`, `[HYP]`, `[PARKED]/[FINAL]`, exactly one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]`.
