## One decision I need from you

I made no mutating requests, so the gateway `PUT` is **unconfirmed end-to-end**, and the DCR report's live evidence (`POST /oauth2/register`, `POST /oauth2/token`) is **carried forward unverified** — its body is intact but I could not re-prove liveness under the passive-only constraint. Both are honest to submit as-is, but the DCR one carries more risk of being stale.

Confirming Medium+ on the gateway finding requires sending one real `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{id}` against a checkout the attacker doesn't own — that needs an authorized SumUp test checkout and authorization to mutate. Want me to (a) leave both as provisional for manual submission to `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`, (b) re-verify only the DCR endpoint liveness with minimal `GET`s, or (c) escalate to request mutation authorization?

One durable lesson worth carrying forward: treat every prior-cycle file path, line count, and hash as unverified until `ls`/`sha256sum` in the current act — this cycle proved those claims were synthesized rather than measured.
