## Objective
- Continue the SumUp bug-bounty hunt from `phase=POC`, `target=api` and return only the required 8-step structured blocks.
- Preserve the two defensible findings and route their reports for human submission without reviving refuted leads.

## Important Details
- Scope: SumUp-owned assets only; submission channel is `bugs.olivermaicher.eu` per `scope.yml:4`.
- Live work must remain passive-first, `<=1 rps`, and GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; no mutating tests or customer-data access.
- Reject out-of-scope/hardening-only classes, including clickjacking without impact, TLS hygiene, descriptive headers, permissive CORS without credential capability, and router differences without data exposure.
- Workspace has re-materialized 41+ times. Start with `ls`; write reports and calculate `wc`/`sha256sum` in the same command before claiming they exist.
- Gateway finding: `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` is 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`; no `X-Frame-Options`/CSP `frame-ancestors`; inbound handler never reads `event.origin`; `payment_type !== "card"` skips the cooperating-frame gate and can trigger `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{id}`. No exfiltration path is proven.
- Gateway session caveat: `X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id` is URL-derived resource identity, not a secret; backend acceptance/privilege gain remains bounded rather than proven.
- Staging DCR: unauthenticated `POST https://auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` returns a client, and `client_secret_post` client-credentials mints a JWT with empty `scp` and attacker-controlled `aud`; prod lacks DCR and prod/staging JWKS have zero `kid` overlap.
- Stable `api.sumup.com` GET/OPTIONS surfaces should not be re-probed; only a live bearer can resolve remaining authorization questions.

## Work State
### Completed
- Finalized `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` as a Medium, passive, confidence-90 cross-origin messenger finding.
- Finalized staging DCR as Low-Medium, passive, confidence-85, staging-only.
- Last recorded gateway report: `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` — 239 lines, 10,083 B, sha256 `41ec5aabbfb36fb9460d8cc18d955cdd0a4dc050c31b4c1f0ce349d16e4ab5f3`.
- Last recorded DCR report: `reports/auth-sam-app-ro-dynamic-registration.md` — 132 lines, 7,172 B, sha256 `ffffbc027e7fb852507054340a246e4e968bf17868dd2175fe976c4ff5b6fdb1`.
- Retired `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` as an IDOR: application routing was real, but 35 identifier/credential responses were invariant with no capability differential.
- Closed Contentful preview-token leak after token rotation; old `reports/contentful-preview-token-leak.md` claims are invalid.

### Active
- Human submission of the gateway and staging-DCR reports remains pending.
- The `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` lead is contradictory and stale: some records claim a 181 B application reflector, while later controls identify a 68 B Vercel platform 404. Do not submit it without re-reading current bytes.
- Program risk is currently 88, driven by the gateway finding and staging DCR.

### Blocked
- No repository submission mechanism exists; disclosure must occur manually at `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Report files may disappear between cycles because the workspace is volatile.
- Remaining API authorization/audience questions require a valid bearer or merchant session and cannot be resolved passively.

