## Objective
- Act as a bug bounty analyst for SumUp (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a 7-step structured cycle (DELTA → PRIORITIZE → HYPOTHESES → SELF-CRITIQUE → NEXT → LEARN → RISK) over passive-first recon on in-scope SumUp assets.
- Current phase: POC, target "api"; goal is to produce verified, fileable reports and hand off submission to a human.

## Important Details
- Passive-first rule: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps; no mutating tests against live customer data; AUTH_HELPED/HUMAN_ONLY flagged when passive can't decide.
- Out-of-scope classes enforced: clickjacking without demonstrated exploit, TLS/SSL best practice, scanner output without PoC, header/banner leaks, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, etc. (scope.yml).
- Disclosure via bugs.olivermaicher.eu (scope.yml:4); no submission mechanism exists in repo (`scripts/sync-issues.py`, `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` mirror leads only).
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles (43 consecutive): artifacts written in cycle N do NOT persist to N+1; always open with `ls` before referencing any `[NEW]` file; write + `sha256sum` must be one act (heredoc in same command).
- Every code citation must be re-read from served bytes, not carried from prior summaries — recurring errors caught this way: the checkoutId gate is a STATIC literal `ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i` (`le=e=>ue.test(e)`), NOT `new RegExp(a.pattern)`.
- Gateway frame-access gate sits inside `if("card"===a.payment_type)` — `Ce(r.frames)`/`if(!d.length)return` skipped when payment_type ≠ "card".
- `origin` param in hosted.js is used ONLY outbound (`t.postMessage(e, n||"")` with `n=document.referrer`); inbound filter is `d=e=>e.type===o.TYPE` (`TYPE:"SumUpCard"`, `ACTION_MESSAGE:"message"`); `grep 'event\.'` = 0.
- Byte-stable surfaces must NOT be re-probed (27+ cycles zero yield): api.sumup.com quartet (payment-methods, RFC 9728 metadata, apple-pay GET 404, prod JWKS 8-kid), auth.sam-app.ro register GET 404.
- DCR re-verification requires POSTing `/oauth2/register` (creates live client) — deliberately skipped; reproduction dates 2026-09-06 → 2026-10-05 given instead.
- Retired/refuted leads (do not re-open): api.sumup.com/v0.2/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods 92-conf IDOR (35 identical responses); js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id} (68B Vercel 404, 4/4 credential differentials failed); pos-payment path-shape 403 enum (negative control same); iso20022 routing divergence (routing note, not vuln); Contentful preview token (rotated 401); mcp wildcard CORS (hardening only).
