[HYP] auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register — unauthenticated RFC 7591 DCR mints issuer-signed staging JWTs
class: OATH
asset: auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register
confidence: 85
reasoning: POST → 201 client_id+client_secret with caller-chosen redirect_uris, no auth/approval; advertised in the server's own discovery `registration_endpoint`. Absent in prod (auth.sumup.com/register 404 GET/POST/OPTIONS). client_credentials+client_secret_post → 200 JWT, iss=auth.sam-app.ro, scp="" empty, aud attacker-influenced; accepted as credential by api.sam-app.ro (structured problem+json 404 vs plain edge 404 unauthenticated). Controls that hold: scope pinned empty (requesting `openid` → invalid_scope), PKCE required, per-client redirect allowlist enforced (401 on mismatch), no RFC 7592 management (404), staging client rejected invalid_client at api.sam-app.ro/authorize. Containment: prod JWKS 8 keys vs staging 11 entries/9 unique, ZERO kid overlap.
evidence_needed: None further for a staging-posture finding — reproduction commands are in the report. The one open question (staging→prod client-provenance sync) needs internal access.
verify_steps: POST https://auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register {redirect_uris:["https://attacker.example/cb"],client_name:"poc"} → 201 client_id/secret → POST /oauth2/token grant_type=client_credentials&client_id&client_secret → 200 JWT (scp empty) → GET https://api.sam-app.ro/v0.1/merchants/{code} with Bearer → structured problem+json vs plain 404. NOT re-run this cycle (creates a live client).
impact: Anonymous self-provisioned credentials plus free zero-authority staging JWT minting. No privilege escalation, no production pivot — key-level isolation verified. Low–Medium, staging posture only.
testability: PASSIVE (repeatedly reproduced 2026-09-06 → 2026-10-05); AUTH_HELPED for the prod-sync question.
[HYP] mcp.sumup.com/mcp — kid-optional try-all on the production bearer verifier
class: AUTH
asset: mcp.sumup.com/mcp
confidence: 70
reasoning: Four-class unauthenticated kid/alg oracle (`no applicable key` / `signature verification failed` / `Unsupported "alg" value` for HS256+none / `multiple matching keys` when kid omitted). Prod trust store accepts exactly its 8 published kids; 22 others absent, 0 undeclared. Alg allowlist {RS256, EdDSA}; HS256 and none explicitly rejected.
evidence_needed: A concrete exploitation path. None exists — no JWKS pollution vector, no cross-env key reuse (zero kid overlap).
verify_steps: POST https://mcp.sumup.com/mcp with RS256 JWT omitting kid → "multiple matching keys"; alg=HS256 → "Unsupported alg value"; unknown kid → "no applicable key".
impact: Hardening deviation only (RFC 8725 §3.11 widened verification surface). No key or alg confusion bypass. Severity Low/informational.
testability: HUMAN_ONLY — cannot reach report class without an exploit that does not exist.
