[RISK] sumup: 74 — Up2 from 72. Gains: both final reports now exist on disk with hashes taken in the same act that wrote them, so the delivery blocker that dominated the last cycle is resolved; and every gateway citation was re-derived from bytes this cycle rather than inherited, which has now caught the same recurring error four separate times. I am NOT claiming delivery is done — nothing is submitted, 43 cycles have produced no disclosure, and both artifacts can vanish before morning. The residual risk is concentrated in one honest weakness of my own: the gateway report's Medium rests on a demonstrated *request*, not a demonstrated *commit*. If SumUp's API enforces `Sumup-Product-Origin` server-side, the PoC stops at the edge and the honest severity is lower than filed. I have written that as an explicit non-claim in §6 rather than letting a triager discover it, but a human may still reasonably rate it Low. That is the correct risk to carry, and it is not reducible without a merchant test credential.
