## Objective
- Act as a senior bug bounty analyst for SumUp (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a 7-step per-cycle hunt (DELTA → PRIORITIZE → HYPOTHESES → SELF-CRITIQUE → NEXT → LEARN → RISK) emitting only structured blocks.
- Current phase: POC on target "api"; ultimate goal is filing the two verified reports for the gateway postMessage and auth.sam-app.ro DCR findings.

## Important Details
- Passive-first rule: live probes ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; no mutating tests against customer data; POSTing auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register creates a live OAuth client and was deliberately skipped.
- Out-of-scope classes include clickjacking-without-exploit, SSL/TLS, header/banner leaks, scanner output without POC; scope.yml:4 defines disclosure via bugs.olivermaicher.eu.
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles (~43 times): artifacts written in cycle N do NOT persist to N+1; any inherited file claim/hash is unproven until `ls`+`wc`+`sha256sum` in the current cycle; write+hash must be one act (heredoc in same command as sha256sum).
- Key verified facts:
  - gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js: 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`; no `event.origin` handling (grep 0), no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors; `origin` param used only outbound `t.postMessage(e, n||"*")`; inbound filter `d=e=>e.type===o.TYPE`; frame-access gate skipped when `payment_type !== "card"`; checkoutId gate is STATIC `ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i` (NOT `new RegExp(a.pattern)`); PoC envelope: `TYPE:"SumUpCard"`, `ACTION_MESSAGE:"message"`, `variant:"hostedfield"`, `form--submit`; `X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id` injected unconditionally by `Te`, `Sumup-Product-Origin` conditional on `fe` (host-pinned checkout.sumup.com/pay/{id}); `sdk.js` 291,877 B, sha256 `0fae546ae34ee5e97cf0c3107d87adaa79129983d423bce6cf9a0fc19916c7bd` shows same defect (systematic across both bundles).
  - auth.sam-app.ro: unauthenticated RFC 7591 DCR (POST → 201), mints JWTs with empty scp + attacker-controlled aud; containment controls: ZERO prod/staging kid overlap (prod 8 keys, staging 11 entries = 9 unique due to 2 duplicates), empty pinned scope, no prod route; prod/staging AS metadata differ only by registration_endpoint; prod sync path UNTESTED.
  - api.sumup.com passive surface exhausted (27+ stable cycles); payment-methods endpoint is param+credential-invariant 404/58B stub; 92-confidence IDOR RETIRED; js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id} REFUTED (68B Vercel 404, 4/4 credential differentials failed) — do not re-open.
  - mcp.sumup.com/mcp: JWT alg:none/HS256 rejected, allowlist {RS256, EdDSA}; kid-optional try-all is hardening-only (PARKED, conf 70-75).
- Reports to submit (hashes from cycle 43 write-act, must re-verify first): `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` (268 L / 12,582 B / a12c3fc9d92210666939decabae215705732ad0db1609a42e1725267732a7238) and `reports/auth-sam-app-ro-dynamic-registration.md` (170 L / 8,570 B / 491a3804f88c44c5eecfbd8ea59fa40254ab9dc743c384dc77e6a2a97d6c96fa). Fill `[fill in program handle before sending]` reporter line in both.
- Scope.yml rejects "clickjacking without demonstrated exploit" — gateway report framed as demonstrated state-changing PUT, not framing.
- Known self-corrections: gateway report §6 contains explicit non-claim (Medium rests on demonstrated *request*, not *commit*; Sumup-Product-Origin server-side enforcement unknown); DCR report marks prod sync UNTESTED, sam-app.ro ownership as triager's call.

## Work State
### Completed
- Two final reports written + verified in same act in cycle 43; gateway evidence re-derived from served bytes (grep 0 for event.origin, framing headers 0).
- Two [FINAL] leads: (1) gateway postMessage forged checkout PUT — conf 92, PASSIVE, Medium; (2) auth.sam-app.ro DCR — conf 85, PASSIVE, Low–Medium staging-only.
- Self-critiques done: CORS claims on js.sumup.com/api and mcp.sumup.com rejected (hardening-only); iso20022 routing divergence rejected (not a security finding); pos-payment path sweep rejected (no negative control); Contentful token leak closed (rotated 401).

### Active
- Phase POC, target "api"; latest cycle emitted [NEXT] HUMAN for report submission.
- Risk score: 74 (Up2); residual risk = gateway Medium rests on demonstrated request not commit.

### Blocked
- HUMAN submission to bugs.olivermaicher.eu has not happened in 43+ cycles; nothing filed (valid-bugs.md count 0/1 historically, file reverts each re-materialization).
- mcp.sumup.com kid-optional lead PARKED: no exploit path exists (HUMAN_ONLY).
- iso20022 POST probing forbidden by passive-only rule.

## Next Move
1. HUMAN: confirm `ls` + `sha256sum` on `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` and `reports/auth-sam-app-ro-dynamic-registration.md`, fill the `[fill in program handle before sending]` reporter line, submit both to bugs.olivermaicher.eu per scope.yml:4.
2. If continuing agent-side: open with `ls` on reports/ first (43 re-materializations), re-verify hosted.js byte-identity before any gateway claim, avoid re-probing byte-stable api.sumup.com/auth.sam-app.ro surfaces (zero yield), and pursue breadth (unmapped CT hosts) rather than depth on closed leads.

## Relevant Files
- `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md`: primary deliverable for gateway postMessage finding (expect 268 L / 12,582 B / a12c3fc9… if persisted).
- `reports/auth-sam-app-ro-dynamic-registration.md`: primary deliverable for DCR staging finding (expect 170 L / 8,570 B / 491a3804… if persisted).
- `reports/valid-bugs.md`: running-count ledger; expected baseline 79-line / 7,384 B / sha256 `282390f8…` pre-append state.
- `scope.yml`: line 4 defines disclosure channel (bugs.olivermaicher.eu) and rejected classes.
- `scripts/sync-issues.py`, `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml`: mirror leads only — no submission mechanism exists in repo.
- `inventory/sumup.md`: seed inventory (9 hosts) plus recon history.
- `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` / `gateway.sumup.com/sdk.js`: source of all gateway citations; verify by GET before quoting.
Continue if you have next steps, or stop and ask for clarification if you are unsure how to proceed.
