## Objective
- Act as a senior bug-bounty analyst for the SumUp program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a 7-step cycle (DELTA → PRIORITIZE → HYPOTHESES → SELF-CRITIQUE → NEXT → LEARNING → RISK) with passive-first, read-only probes (≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only).
- Current state: `{"phase": "POC", "target": "api"}`; two final reports written but submission blocked on a human.

## Important Details
- In-scope: only assets from `scope.yml` + `inventory/sumup.md` (SumUp Group company-owned infra, payment platforms, APIs, POS, cloud, domains).
- Rejected classes explicitly include clickjacking-without-exploit, SSL/TLS best practice, header/banner leaks (e.g. `x-envoy-decorator-operation`), descriptive errors, OPTIONS/TRACE findings, wildcard-CORS-without-capability-differential.
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles (43 confirmed cycles): artifacts written in cycle N do NOT persist to N+1. Rule: `open with ls` first; write+`sha256sum` must be one act (heredoc + hash in same command) before any `[NEW]` file claim; a file claim without in-context hash is unproven.
- No submission mechanism in repo — `scope.yml:4` declares disclosure via bugs.olivermaicher.eu; `scripts/sync-issues.py` + `.github/workflows/sync-issues.yml` mirror leads only.
- Top-2 ranked hypotheses: [90] `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` cross-origin postMessage checkout-write; [85] `auth.sam-app.ro/oauth2/register` unauthenticated RFC 7591 DCR.
- Gateway key facts: `hosted.js` 26,839 B / sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`; `grep 'event\.'` → 0; `origin` param used only outbound (`t.postMessage(e, n||"*")`); inbound filter `e.type===o.TYPE`; frame-access gate inside `if("card"===a.payment_type)` branch; checkoutId gate is STATIC UUID v1–v5 literal `ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i` (NOT `new RegExp(a.pattern)`); PoC envelope `TYPE:"SumUpCard"`, `ACTION_MESSAGE:"message"`, `variant:"hostedfield"`, `form--submit` = `$`. `sdk.js` 291,877 B / sha256 `0fae546a...` shares the missing-origin-validation defect.
- DCR key facts: staging JWKS = 11 entries / 9 unique keys (2 duplicates) vs prod 8; ZERO kid overlap; staging discovery advertises 20 `scopes_supported`; prod client-provenance-sync path is UNTESTED (not "safe"); DCR report deliberately not re-probed (POST would create a live OAuth client).
- Retired/refuted leads (do NOT re-open): `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` 92-conf IDOR (35 byte-identical responses); `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` (68 B Vercel 404, 4/4 credential diffs failed); `pos-payment.sumup.com` path-shape enum (nonsense path → same 403); Contentful preview token (rotated 401, report file never existed); iso20022 routing divergence (recon note only).
- Blocked surfaces: byte-stable `api.sumup.com` quartet (27+ cycles, only a live bearer discriminates); `auth.sam-app.ro` prod-relay leg unfalsifiable passively.
- Some KB entries conflict (e.g. payment-methods 200 `{"card"}` vs 404; js BFF 181 B vs 68 B) — later REJECTED entries are authoritative.

