- Top finding (conf 90): `gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` cross-origin postMessage → attacker drives framed PCI card-entry iframe to `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{uuid}`. bundle 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`. No `event.origin` read (`grep -o 'event\.'` → 0); origin param used only outbound `t.postMessage(e, n||"*")`; frame-access gate `Ce(r.frames)` nested under `if("card"===a.payment_type)` (attacker opts out); checkoutId gate is STATIC literal `ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i` (NOT `new RegExp(a.pattern)` — recurring KB error, do not repeat). No exfiltration path (outbound reply throws on full-URL referrer).
