# SumUp — gateway.sumup.com hosted-fields cross-origin postMessage drives checkout writes

- **Status:** ready to file
- **Report channel:** bugs.olivermaicher.eu (`scope.yml:4`)
- **Class:** MISCONFIG / missing origin validation on a cross-origin message channel
- **Severity:** Medium (bounded; see Impact)
- **Evidence basis:** all citations re-derived from served bytes on 2026-10-06 UTC

## Target

`https://gateway.sumup.com/hosted.js` — the script that constructs SumUp's hosted
card-entry iframe (a PCI card-collection surface).

- Served: `200`, `access-control-allow-origin: *`
- Response headers: **no** `X-Frame-Options`, **no** `Content-Security-Policy`
  (frame-ancestors absent)
- Bytes: `26,839 B`
- SHA-256: `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`
- `grep -c 'event\.' hosted.js` → **0**
- `grep -c 'X-Frame-Options\|frame-ancestors' hosted.js` → **0**

The same defect class is present in the sibling first-party bundle on the same
host: `https://gateway.sumup.com/sdk.js`, `291,877 B`, SHA-256
`0fae546ae34ee5e97cf0c3107d87adaa79129983d423bce6cf9a0fc19916c7bd`,
`grep -ci 'event\.origin'` → **0**, also served `access-control-allow-origin: *`.

## The bug

### 1. Inbound messages are never origin-checked

