## Objective
- Act as a bug bounty ANALYST for the SumUp program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a 7-step per-cycle analysis (DELTA → PRIORITIZE → HYPOTHESES → SELF-CRITIQUE → NEXT → LEARN → RISK) producing only structured blocks.
- Current phase: POC, target: api; goal is to move two validated findings from evidence to submission.

## Important Details
- Scope: only SumUp Group company-owned infra per scope.yml + inventory/sumup.md; passive-first live probing (GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps); no mutating tests against live customer data.
- Out-of-scope classes include clickjacking-without-demonstrated-exploit, descriptive headers only, OPTIONS/TRACE findings, SSL/TLS best practice, username enumeration.
- Workspace is re-materialized between cycles (43+ times): artifacts written in cycle N do NOT persist to N+1; `valid-bugs.md` always reverts to baseline 79-line/7,384-B/`282390f8` state. Always open with `ls` before trusting any prior `[NEW]` file claim.
- Write discipline: heredoc + `sha256sum` in the SAME command is the only reliable file-creation method; a `[NEW]` line quoting line count/hash without an in-context hash is unproven.
- Byte-stable surfaces (do NOT re-probe): api.sumup.com quartet (27+ stable cycles), auth.sam-app.ro register GET 404 — only a live bearer discriminates.
- Do NOT re-open: `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` (68B Vercel platform 404, 4/4 credential differentials failed — authoritative refutation), `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR (RETIRED: param- and credential-invariant 404/58B stub), pos-payment path-sweep enum (refuted by negative control), iso20022 routing divergence (routing observation ≠ vulnerability), Contentful preview token (rotated 401; report file never existed).
- DCR re-verification requires POST `/oauth2/register` (creates live OAuth client) — deliberately NOT re-probed; treat as already-verified.
- Gateway PoC envelope constants (from served bytes): `TYPE:"SumUpCard"`, `ACTION_MESSAGE:"message"`, `variant:"hostedfield"`, `form--submit` = `$`.
- Gateway UUID gate is a STATIC literal: `ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i` — never `new RegExp(a.pattern)`.
- Report framing constraint: scope.yml rejects bare clickjacking; gateway report must be framed as demonstrated state-changing PUT under attacker control (CSRF-class), severity capped pending backend acceptance evidence.

## Work State
### Completed
- Gateway finding fully evidenced: `hosted.js` 26,839 B, sha256 `1302f1d6a8fa330a71e50647be0281e4b977a198cbf27e0fd59cbecc9f220873`, byte-identical across cycles; `grep -o 'event\.'` → 0; no framing headers; inbound filter `d=e=>e.type===o.TYPE` only; frame-access gate skipped when `payment_type !== "card"`; `Te` injects `X-SumUp-Widget-Session-Id` unconditionally ("undefined" string when absent); live PoC (netlog + iframe console) shows cross-origin `form--submit` drives `PUT /v0.2/checkouts/{uuid}`.
- DCR finding fully evidenced (staging posture): POST → 201 client_id+secret; empty scope forced; PKCE required; per-client redirect allowlist; `client_secret_post` works, `client_secret_basic` fails (auth method not enforced); attacker-set `aud`; bindings: prod JWKS 8 keys vs staging 11 entries/9 unique, ZERO kid overlap; prod `/oauth2/register` → 404; staging tokens rejected at mcp.sumup.com.
- KB corrections applied to DCR report: staging JWKS 11 entries = 9 unique (two `public:*` kids duplicated); staging discovery advertises 20 `scopes_supported`; prod client-provenance-sync path stated as explicitly UNTESTED.
- Last cycle (2026-10-07 05:31): both reports reconstructed and confirmed on disk in same act — `reports/gateway-hostedfields-cross-origin-messenger.md` (174 L / 8,593 B / sha256 `4291c1281cae2d4f0ad3a273b42e65798…`); `reports/auth-sam-app-ro-dynamic-registration.md` also written.
- Current ranked leads: [90] gateway cross-origin postMessage checkout-write; [85] auth.sam-app.ro DCR; [75] mcp.sumup.com JWT kid-optional try-all.

