- 2026-09-30 ACCEPTED OTHER @ differential matrices: **the anomalous cell is the one most likely to be transient, not the one most likely to be a discovery.** My re-verification of the endpoint I was retiring produced a 500/0B on credential shape 7 of 7 — exactly the shape a "credential differential" claim needs — and the prior cycle's KB entry contains a finding built on precisely such a reading. Re-running the *identical* token 3× returned 404/58B every time. The generalisable rule is narrower than "repeat your probes": a matrix is a sampling device, and a lone outlier in it carries no more weight than a lone outlier anywhere else. An input that produces a novel response must be re-sent *verbatim* before it is believed, because the alternative is filing a transient as a mechanism. This is the third time in this program that a single uncontrolled reading became a multi-cycle lead — the first two were the 500/0B and a fabricated UUID gate, and both were killed only by an explicit negative control.
