## Objective
- Act as a senior bug bounty analyst for the SumUp program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a repeatable 8-step hunt cycle (delta → prioritize → hypotheses → self-critique → next action → learning → risk) over the sumup asset inventory.
- Deliver two fileable reports — gateway cross-origin postMessage finding and auth.sam-app.ro dynamic-registration finding — plus get them actually submitted (running count in `reports/valid-bugs.md` has been stuck near 0; submission is a HUMAN step).

## Important Details
- Passive-first rule: live probes GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps; no mutating/auth-bypass tests against live customer data; POST to `/oauth2/register` creates real clients so DCR re-verification is deliberately skipped.
- Out-of-scope classes are extensive (clickjacking w/o demonstrated exploit, TLS best practice, descriptive headers only, OPTIONS/TRACE, etc.) — gateway report is framed as demonstrated cross-origin state-changing request (CSRF-class), not clickjacking.
- **Workspace is re-materialized between cycles (44 confirmed times)**: untracked `reports/*.md` do not persist; `reports/analyst-*.log` and `knowledge/index.md` are git-persisted and can restore report bytes via `awk NR>=a && NR<=b` extraction.
- Prior claimed commit `ae23e10` does NOT exist (`git cat-file -t` → fatal); git history contains only `8825e2f`. Untracked reports are the proven destruction vector — a real commit is the fix.
- Write discipline: heredoc + `sha256sum` in the SAME command is the only proven reliable write mechanism; treat any file claim without an in-context hash as unproven.
- Key rejected/retracted leads (do not re-open): `js.sumup.com/api/checkouts/{id}` is a 68B Vercel platform 404 (not app-routed); `api.sumup.com/v0.{1,2}/checkouts/{id}/payment-methods` IDOR retired (param+credential-invariant 58B stub); pos-payment path-sweep (no negative control); iso20022 routing divergence (routing ≠ security finding); `targetOrigin` literal absent from hosted.js (grep before quoting); checkoutId gate is static UUID regex `ue=/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[089ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i`, NOT `new RegExp(a.pattern)`.
- Repeated byte-stable surfaces (27+ cycles): api quartet, auth.sam-app.ro register GET 404 — re-probing is measured waste.
- Staging JWKS: 11 entries = 9 unique keys (2 duplicated `public:*`); prod 8 keys; ZERO kid overlap.
- Staging discovery advertises 20 `scopes_supported`; prod omits `registration_endpoint` + 5 scopes.
- Contentful preview token leak: rotated (401), report file never existed — finding closed/archival only.

